Q: Unset relative date format for GTK Open/Save dialog A: <p>Guess nobody cares about this crap. I kept fighting against this for decades, the date is still mixing all sorts of formats, even if is not the worse &quot;relative date&quot;.</p>
<p>I tried:</p>
<ul>
<li>changing <code>LC_*</code> to all <code>en_IE</code>, <code>en_DK</code> ...</li>
<li>hacking  /usr/share/i18n/locales/nn_LL</li>
<li>all sorts of <code>gsettings</code> magic</li>
<li>all sorts of stuff like <code>env GTK_OVERRIDE_DATE_FORMAT</code></li>
</ul>
<p>none of these affects the (gtk) Open File dialog, because it's hardcoded.</p>
<p>update, ok, fixed. just grab gtk source code, find <code>Translators:</code> part of <code>gtkfilechooserwidget.c</code>,  get rigd of the related part and build and replace your libgtk3...</p>
<pre class="lang-c prettyprint-override"><code>  /* Translators: see g_date_time_format() for details on the format */
#if 0
  if (days_ago &lt; 1)
    {
      if (priv-&gt;show_time)
        format = &quot;&quot;;
      else if (clock_format == CLOCK_FORMAT_24)
        format = _(&quot;%H:%M&quot;);
      else
        format = _(&quot;%l:%M %p&quot;);
    }
  else if (days_ago &lt; 2)
    {
      format = _(&quot;Yesterday&quot;);
    }
  else if (days_ago &lt; 7)
    {
      format = &quot;%a&quot;; /* Days from last week */
    }
  else if (g_date_time_get_year (now) == g_date_time_get_year (time))
    {
      /* xgettext:no-c-format */
      format = _(&quot;%-e %b&quot;);
    }
  else
    {
      format = N_(&quot;%-e %b %Y&quot;);
    }
#endif
  format = _(&quot;%Y-%m-%d&quot;); // or your local format or system's format
  date_str = g_date_time_format (time, format);
</code></pre>

Q: Delete all users from firebase auth console A: <h2><strong>2026 Update: Tested</strong></h2>
<pre><code>setInterval(() =&gt; {
  try {
    // Step 1: click the 3-dot menu (edit button)
    const menuBtn = document.querySelector(
      '.edit-account-button.mat-mdc-menu-trigger'
    );
    if (!menuBtn) return;
    menuBtn.click();

    // Step 2: wait a bit for menu to open
    setTimeout(() =&gt; {
      const menuItems = document.querySelectorAll(
        '.mat-mdc-menu-item'
      );

      if (!menuItems.length) return;

      // Usually last item = Delete
      const deleteBtn = menuItems[menuItems.length - 1];
      deleteBtn.click();

      // Step 3: wait for confirm dialog
      setTimeout(() =&gt; {
        const confirmBtn = document.querySelector(
          '.confirm-button.mat-warn'
        );
        if (confirmBtn) confirmBtn.click();
      }, 500);

    }, 500);

  } catch (e) {
    console.error(&quot;Error:&quot;, e);
  }
}, 2000);
</code></pre>
